T16 analysis (generated by tests/T16/analyse.py from the shipped evidence; nothing typed). W1 (T11's / T14's / T15's inputs) 2014-09-01 -> 2019-01-02, W2 (T08's inputs, extended) 2019-01-02 -> 2026-11-20
Books: SCMO_0003, SCMO_0007, SCMO_0010, SCMO_0029. Costs 0.0, 20.8, 50.0 bps round trip (primary 20.8). No null, no chance claim (waiver).

====================================================================================================
4.0 The rules and the runs in words (read this first)
====================================================================================================
States, read every Friday: IN = the Nifty 100, Midcap 100 and Smallcap 100 weekly supertrend SIGNs are all BUY (the book holds the parent's basket); otherwise the switch is OUT and the book holds a sleeve: OUT-BUY = OUT and the weekly MAUc1 gold SIGN is BUY; OUT-SELL = OUT and MAUc1 is SELL. B = the indices whose own SIGN is BUY in an OUT week and k = how many (0, 1 or 2; 3 would be IN). Base sleeve: 50 = 50% GOLDBEES / 50% cash; 80 = 80% GOLDBEES / 20% cash when gold is BUY and 20% / 80% when gold is SELL. Cash = the LBES liquid-ETF level. The ten rules differ only in what they hold in OUT-SELL. A rule id is <base>-<its OUT-SELL holding>, such as 50-all; a bare suffix (-orig, -half, -liq, -idx, -all) means that holding on both bases.

Rules (what each book holds in each state; they differ only in OUT-SELL):
  50-orig  base 50/50.  IN: the parent's own basket.  OUT-BUY: 50% GOLDBEES, 50% liquid ETF (cash).  OUT-SELL: 50% GOLDBEES, 50% cash (the same sleeve).  Role: comparator; regression.  From: T06 / T11 Part A.
  50-half  base 50/50.  IN: the parent's own basket.  OUT-BUY: 50% GOLDBEES, 50% cash.  OUT-SELL: 50% the parent's basket, 50% GOLDBEES.  Role: comparator; regression.  From: T14.
  50-liq   base 50/50.  IN: the parent's own basket.  OUT-BUY: 50% GOLDBEES, 50% cash.  OUT-SELL: 100% liquid ETF.  Role: comparator; regression.  From: T14.
  50-idx   base 50/50.  IN: the parent's own basket.  OUT-BUY: 50% GOLDBEES, 50% cash.  OUT-SELL: liquid ETF plus each index whose own SIGN is BUY, in equal parts 1 / (k + 1) (k = how many are BUY), rebalanced when that set changes.  Role: comparator; regression.  From: T15.
  50-all   base 50/50.  IN: the parent's own basket.  OUT-BUY: 50% GOLDBEES, 50% cash.  OUT-SELL: 25% each of Nifty 100, Midcap 100, Smallcap 100 and the liquid ETF, whatever each index's own SIGN is; set on entry, left to drift, traded only when the book leaves OUT-SELL.  Role: NEW.  From: T16 (Manu, 2026-11-26).
  80-orig  base 80/20.  IN: the parent's own basket.  OUT-BUY: 80% GOLDBEES, 20% cash.  OUT-SELL: 20% GOLDBEES, 80% cash.  Role: comparator; regression.  From: T08 / T11 Part B.
  80-half  base 80/20.  IN: the parent's own basket.  OUT-BUY: 80% GOLDBEES, 20% cash.  OUT-SELL: 50% the parent's basket, 50% GOLDBEES.  Role: comparator; regression.  From: T14.
  80-liq   base 80/20.  IN: the parent's own basket.  OUT-BUY: 80% GOLDBEES, 20% cash.  OUT-SELL: 100% liquid ETF.  Role: comparator; regression.  From: T14.
  80-idx   base 80/20.  IN: the parent's own basket.  OUT-BUY: 80% GOLDBEES, 20% cash.  OUT-SELL: liquid ETF plus each index whose own SIGN is BUY, in equal parts 1 / (k + 1), rebalanced when that set changes.  Role: comparator; regression.  From: T15.
  80-all   base 80/20.  IN: the parent's own basket.  OUT-BUY: 80% GOLDBEES, 20% cash.  OUT-SELL: 25% each of Nifty 100, Midcap 100, Smallcap 100 and the liquid ETF, whatever each index's own SIGN is; set on entry, left to drift, traded only when the book leaves OUT-SELL.  Role: NEW.  From: T16 (Manu, 2026-11-26).

Benchmarks printed beside the rules:
  hold_parent: hold the book's own parent from the first session (no timing; the parent's rebalances only). Role: comparator (benchmark).
  hold_Nifty100, hold_MC100, hold_SC100: buy that price index at the first session's close and hold it, no trades (hold each index alone). Role: comparator (benchmark).
  eq3_index_basket: one third each of Nifty 100, Midcap 100 and Smallcap 100, rebalanced at every weekly decision, 20.8 bps. Role: comparator (benchmark).
  cmix_<rule>  (cmix_50-all, cmix_80-all, ...): the constant mix at that rule's own average shares of parent, GOLDBEES, cash and each index (the mean over the weekly decisions of the rule's target shares), rebalanced at every decision. Role: comparator (benchmark).

Runs and windows (dates from the evidence):
  W1    the parent rebuilt from its baskets and stock prices (no published NAV exists before 2019-01-02). 2014-09-01 -> 2019-01-02, 228 weekly decisions. Role: window. From: T11's / T14's / T15's inputs, pinned.
  W2    the published NAVs' calendar (SCMO_0007 starts two days later). 2019-01-02 -> 2026-11-20, 413 weekly decisions. Role: window. From: T08's inputs, extended from T15's 2026-10-30.
  live  W2's decisions from 2021-11-01, the AA books' live period (R3 on W2). Role: robustness. From: T14.
  R1    round-trip cost 0 and 50 bps instead of 20.8. Role: robustness. From: T14.
  R2    LIQUIDCASE as the cash leg instead of the LBES level (W1 the whole window; W2 from 2024-01-24). Role: robustness. From: T14.
  R3    a later start: W1 from 2015-01-02, W2 live from 2021-11-01, each with its own first state (both start in OUT-SELL). Role: robustness. From: T14.
  R4    leave one OUT-SELL spell out: the two -all rules hold 100% cash in that spell only (as -liq), everything else unchanged. Role: robustness. From: T14 / T15, here applied to -all.
  R5    a fund-cost drag of 0.5 pp a year on each index leg (index prices times (1 - 0.005 / 252) per session). Role: robustness. From: T15.

The six comparisons (each about the -all rule of a base b against the comparator of the same base and book; passes when the stated sign holds in at least 3 of the 4 books; unrounded statistics, 20.8 bps, whole window):
  C1: -all earns more than the original rule (CAGR higher than -orig).
  C2: -all's worst fall no deeper than the original's (max drawdown shallower or equal to -orig).
  C3: holding the three indices adds to holding only cash in the regime (CAGR higher than -liq).
  C4: -all does better than half parent + half GOLDBEES in the regime (CAGR higher than -half).
  C5: ignoring the index signals in the regime earns more than following them (CAGR higher than -idx).
  C6: ignoring the signals does not deepen the worst fall (max drawdown shallower or equal to -idx).

